{
  "id": "book-26",
  "checkpoint": 10,
  "title": "Looking Through the Window",
  "summary": "Enquanto o trem viaja para o norte, Paul observa a paisagem mudar da cidade para o campo e pede uma xícara de chá quente.",
  "audio_url": "/audios/book-26.mp3",
  "word_count_target": 140,
  "story_en": "The train gathers speed as it leaves the noisy city behind. Paul rests his elbow near the window and gazes at the changing landscape. Tall brick buildings slowly give way to wide green fields and quiet farmhouses.\n\nAfter half an hour, an attendant pushes a metal snack cart down the aisle. “Would you like something hot to drink or a fresh snack?” she asks politely.\n\n“Yes, please,” Paul answers. “Could I get a cup of hot tea and a sweet biscuit?”\n\n“Of course,” she smiles, handing him the warm cup and a small plate. “That will be three dollars.”\n\nPaul pays the attendant and takes a slow sip. The warm drink relaxes him. Through the clear glass, he sees the distant outline of the mountain range growing sharper against the blue sky.",
